The in-process server (docs/design/wine-unix.md, section 7; section 9 for
its timeouts).

The server runs in the client's thread, inside the one wasm64 module.
Wine's pipes and fd bookkeeping stay; the socket, the lock, the daemon,
the signals and main_loop don't run.
- Transport (ntdll unix/server.c, server/thread.c): after send_request,
  the client calls inproc_server_request, which reads the request of the
  one server thread whose request pipe holds data (read_request); the
  client then reads the reply as Wine does. An empty reply pipe is a
  server bug.
- Waits (unix/server.c, server/thread.c): a wait_fd read that gets
  EAGAIN waits in green.c (inproc_wait_wakeup); send_thread_wakeup wakes
  the waiters after its write.
- fds (unix/server.c, server/request.c, server/thread.c):
  wine_server_send_fd sends nothing, since both sides share the fd table;
  thread_get_inflight_fd dup()s the client's fd by number;
  send_client_fd queues a dup that wine_server_receive_fd takes.
- Start (unix/server.c, server/request.c): server_init_process calls
  inproc_server_start in place of server_connect; inproc_server_init runs
  create_server_dir, set_current_time, init_memory, init_directories,
  init_threading and init_registry, sets server_start_time as main_loop
  does, and creates the process (msg_fd: a pipe's read end) and its first
  thread as master_socket_poll_event does.
- Memory (server/mapping.c): init_memory uses 4 KiB pages and ranges64
  [0x1_0000_0000, 0x1_7000_0000) (section 4); the server's KUSER pointer
  is 0x7ffe0000.
- Timeouts (server/fd.c, server/registry.c): inproc_server_next_timeout
  and inproc_server_run_timeouts for the scheduler's entries; the next
  timeout skips the registry's periodic save.
- Loud stops: main_loop, receive_fd (only main_loop reads msg_fd), a
  partial reply write (only main_loop would deliver POLLOUT), and
  send_thread_signal of anything but SIGQUIT, which exits (M2: one
  thread, as quit_handler's abort_thread(0) of the last thread).
- The declarations shared by the server and Tempwind's src/ are at the
  end of server/file.h.

